<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30694" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδν-όω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐεδν-</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕδνον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>promise
				for wedding-presents, betroth</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν ἕδνωσε θύγατρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.147
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, of a father, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς κ᾽ αὐτὸς ἐεδνώσαιτο θύγατρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.53
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑδνώσομαί τε θυγατέρ</span>' (<i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδώσομαι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hel.</u>
				933
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Med.
			, of a husband, <i>dower</i> a wife, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				94.47
			</span></i>; simply, <i>marry</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.648
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <i>woo</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				6.3
			</span></i>.</div>
